WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.016
Learn to estimate area by using referents for cm2 or m2 and develop and apply a

00:00:06.016 --> 00:00:09.288
formula for determining area of a rectangle and square

00:00:10.117 --> 00:00:16.295
Estimate the number of 1 cm squared tiles covering a 10 cm by 7 cm rectangle. The

00:00:16.295 --> 00:00:20.293
answer is 70. Each unit square contributes 1 cm squared .

00:00:21.117 --> 00:00:26.368
A display mat has 9 rows with 2 square tiles each. How many square units are covered?

00:00:26.368 --> 00:00:28.839
Pause and solve it in your exercise book.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.177
The answer is 18. 9 times 2 equals 18.
